Package: renewal
Title: Retention, Lifetime and Conversion Statistics for Subscriptions
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Haluk", "Demirhan", email = "support@thecommercium.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Commercium Limited", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Statistics for subscription products with small samples. Fits the
    shifted beta-geometric model of Fader and Hardie (2007) <doi:10.1002/dir.20074> and the
    beta-discrete-Weibull model of Fader et al. (2018) <doi:10.1016/j.intmar.2018.01.002> to
    right-censored subscriber records or cohort counts, and reports survival, retention,
    discounted expected lifetime and residual lifetime with delta-method intervals. Conversion
    rates get Jeffreys intervals, and rates of several groups are pooled with a hierarchical
    beta-binomial model whose hyperparameters are integrated out. Implemented in base R; the
    same specification is implemented in Python and TypeScript and checked against shared,
    high-precision test vectors.
